+## public-api-hash
+* Tracking rustc issue: [#158844](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/158844)
+
+The `-Z public-api-hash` flag passes the same flag to `rustc`, which then reports a hash of
+everything in the metadata of a library that its dependents can observe. When a library is
+dirty only because some of its dependencies were compiled again, and none of them changed
+what the library can observe, Cargo does not compile the library again: it would produce the
+same outputs. Its outputs are marked as up to date instead, and its cached warnings are shown
+like for a fresh library.
+
+For example, a change to the body of a non-generic, non-inline function in one crate no
+longer compiles all the crates that depend on it again; only the crates that link it, such
+as binaries and tests, are linked again.
+
+What a library can observe of a dependency is:
+
+* for a library compiled with `-Z public-api-hash`: its public API hash;
+* for a build script run: its output. Files that the build script writes are tracked like
+  the library's own source files;
+* for anything else, for example a proc macro: whether it was compiled again.
+
+Only crates of type `lib` and `rlib` are skipped. A library with cached diagnostics is
+compiled again when one of them points into a file of another crate, because the public API
+hash leaves out the positions that dependents only use in diagnostics.
+
+```toml
+# .cargo/config.toml
+[unstable]
+public-api-hash = true
+```
+
